    <briefdescription>
<para>Network Failure Scenario 11: Cascading Failures (F &lt; N/3). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tests behavior when multiple nodes fail simultaneously (respects F &lt; N/3).</para>
<para><bold>Setup:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>5-node cluster (tolerate F&lt;2, max 1 failure)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Simulate 2 node failures</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Execution:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Node failure 1: remaining 4 nodes can still achieve quorum (2/3 of 3 needed)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Node failure 2: remaining 3 nodes exactly at quorum boundary</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Attempt additional writes</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If 3rd node fails: quorum lost, no more writes</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Verification:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>After 1 failure: cluster operational</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>After 2 failures: cluster operational (barely)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>After 3+ failures: cluster read-only (quorum lost)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No data loss during failures</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Expected:</bold> Cluster remains operational until quorum lost </para>
    </detaileddescription>
